"gitch found nothing to draw for %@." = "gitch no encontró nada que dibujar para %1$@.";
"gitch graph changes: files that are often committed together, and how often each one changes." = "gitch graph changes: archivos que suelen ir juntos en un commit y cuántas veces cambia cada uno.";
"gitch graph check reads its rules from .gitch/graph.rules in this repository. Create the file with commented-out examples (gitch graph check --init) and open it?" = "gitch graph check lee sus reglas de .gitch/graph.rules en este repositorio. ¿Crear el archivo con ejemplos comentados (gitch graph check --init) y abrirlo?";
"gitch graph diff files: imports added and removed on this branch, and cycles that appeared, grew, shrank or went away." = "gitch graph diff files: imports añadidos y eliminados en esta rama, y ciclos que aparecieron, crecieron, se redujeron o desaparecieron.";
"gitch graph diff modules: module dependencies added and removed on this branch." = "gitch graph diff modules: dependencias de módulos añadidas y eliminadas en esta rama.";
"gitch graph diff tree: folders whose number of files or size changed on this branch." = "gitch graph diff tree: carpetas cuyo número de archivos o tamaño cambió en esta rama.";
"gitch graph files: which file imports which, for TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Go, Rust, Kotlin and Java. Swift files are linked by the type names they use (dashed lines)." = "gitch graph files: qué archivo importa a cuál, para TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Go, Rust, Kotlin y Java. Los archivos Swift se enlazan por los nombres de tipo que usan (líneas discontinuas).";
"gitch graph modules: targets and packages from Package.swift, Tuist, package.json, Cargo, Go and Gradle. Reading Package.swift takes a few seconds." = "gitch graph modules: targets y paquetes de Package.swift, Tuist, package.json, Cargo, Go y Gradle. Leer Package.swift tarda unos segundos.";
"gitch graph tree: folders with their size and number of files." = "gitch graph tree: carpetas con su tamaño y número de archivos.";
"gitch keeps several Git accounts apart: it locks each repository to an account, picks the account by folder or organization, and blocks wrong authors, secrets and force pushes in git hooks, in the terminal, for AI agents and in Gitrochi." = "gitch mantiene separadas varias cuentas de Git: vincula cada repositorio a una cuenta, elige la cuenta por reglas de carpeta u organización y, mediante hooks de Git, impide autores incorrectos, secretos y push forzados, en la terminal, para agentes de IA y en Gitrochi.";
"gitch saves a backup before pull, up, sync, fix, undo and amend, and keeps the 30 most recent." = "gitch guarda una copia antes de pull, up, sync, fix, undo y amend, y conserva las 30 más recientes.";
"gitch sets the commit author to %@ and points origin (and upstream) at %@'s SSH alias, then locks the repository to it." = "gitch establece %1$@ como autor de los commits, apunta origin (y upstream) al alias SSH de %2$@ y vincula el repositorio a esa cuenta.";
"gitch stops requiring %@ for commits and pushes here. The commit author stays as it is." = "gitch dejará de exigir %1$@ para commits y push aquí. El autor de los commits no cambia.";
"gitch sync: brings this branch up to date with the original repository (upstream)." = "gitch sync: pone esta rama al día con el repositorio original (upstream).";
"gitch up: moves this branch onto the latest default branch, or merges it if the branch is already pushed. A backup is saved first." = "gitch up: mueve esta rama sobre la rama predeterminada más reciente, o la fusiona si ya se hizo push. Antes guarda una copia de seguridad.";
"gitch won't check authors, secrets or pushes in this repository until you turn it back on." = "gitch no revisará autores, secretos ni push en este repositorio hasta que lo vuelvas a activar.";
